<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Ask three contractors what ranch fencing costs per foot and you'll get three different answers. Here's the honest version: in 2026, most Central Texas ranch fence runs between <strong>$2.50 and $28 per foot</strong> depending on the fence type, your terrain, and how many corners and gates you need. A basic 5-strand barbed wire fence on flat pasture sits at the low end. A welded <a href="/pipe-fence-waco/">pipe fence</a> along your road frontage sits at the top.</p><p>We build fence every week across Waco, <a href="/fence-builder-china-spring/">China Spring</a>, <a href="/fence-builder-crawford/">Crawford</a>, and the rest of McLennan, Bosque, and Falls counties, so these numbers come from real jobs, not a national average. Below you'll find current per-foot and per-mile pricing for every fence type we install, plus the factors that push a bid up or down. When you're ready for an exact number, call <strong>(509) 351-8404</strong> and we'll walk your line and put it in writing for free.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 56px;"><div style="max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;">
